41
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Andrea Cooperman got in touch with us about last week's podcast.

42
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
We were talking about who leads the leaders

43
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:18,000
And she said: I guess in a way I disagree with the idea that the Scoutmaster and the committee chair dictate the direction of the troop.

44
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Yeah, you do need somebody to make the final decisions and at times to be the fall guy.

45
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,000
But I found I get more out of my adult leaders when I give them the reins.

46
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:31,000
When I take my ego out of the equation, things generally go smoother.

47
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
My way isn't always the right way

48
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:36,000
And I have come to recognize what my weaknesses are

49
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:40,000
And I try to encourage other adults to show me new ways of taking care of business.

50
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,000
When I ask them, how can we make this better,

51
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
What do you think?

52
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
And someone says that they'll take care of things,

53
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,000
I say awesome,

54
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,000
How about it?

55
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,000
And how can I help?

56
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Well, thanks for that, Andrea.

57
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:55,000
You know, I don't think we disagree at all, because both of these things are true.

58
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:00,000
The Scoutmaster and the committee chair are supposed to get together and make things happen.

59
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:05,000
The committee chair, in the way that things are set up, has really got the final word on things.

60
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
If it comes to that- and let's hope it doesn't right-

61
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:11,000
I mean everybody should be able to get together and agree on things.

62
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,000
You want to build consensus.

63
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
You want everybody. you know: hey, we're doing Scouts,

64
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Let's be happy.

65
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:22,000
The style that you apply when you are in that position ought to be exactly as you described.

66
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Let people take care of their responsibilities in the best way that they possibly can,

67
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,000
And that might be different than you first think it should be.

68
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Like you said, Andrea, give them the reins,

69
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Let them run with something,

70
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Let them be happier.

71
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:38,000
You're going to have that responsibility taken care of. what could be better, right?

72
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,000
I heard from John Patrick Hickey.

73
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:44,000
You said thanks so much for all the great things you share to advance scouting-

74
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Great and fun stuff.

75
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Thanks, John

76
